# Profile notes: primary claims use the did:demos:agent ClaimReference profile
# (src/catalog/claimRef.ts), which the pinned revision does not yet define. It comes from
# DACS-Standard #296, merged into `next` at 725fa78bd124a7adb65df27adee376d5d44a4bd7; its fixture
# is vendored below. Its keys are Ed25519, so artifacts signed with ecdsa-secp256k1 or
# sr1-aggregate cannot be verified under this profile and are not published or counted.
# Recorded deviations (test/standard-vectors.test.ts pins each):
#   §8.5.2 checks 5-6 need the CommitmentRecord's anchored committedAt, which a bundle does not
#     reference: a session whose listing sets deadlineSecAfterCommit or validity.notAfter is
#     indeterminate and never counted.
#   CD-1: a non-canonical amount (e.g. "95.00") is rejected rather than canonicalised (fail-closed).
#   agreement-listing-v0.1 `fractional-pct-out` expects reject; the §8.5.2 text (round to the CD-1
#     digits of bandCenter) accepts it, and the Directory follows the text.
#   SB-1: pinned evm/x402 refs omit logIndex; Solana refs omit instructionIndex. These refs are
#     error and never counted. AP2, htlc-* and liquidity-tank refs have no SB-1 key format and are
#     likewise uncounted (HTLC-5 session binding is not an SB-1 key). Every legacy SDK evm-erc20
#     or x402 deal is uncounted because its TxRef lacks the event index; only legacy pay-dem keys.
#   Authoritative bundle absence: the Demos mapping declares no absence-evidence policy. Both
#     absence sets below run; their policy-qualified one-sided pass/include cases deliberately
#     remain indeterminate/excluded. No Directory endpoint authenticates those projected proofs.
#   Vet admission resolves historical IdentityBundle bytes and checks the presentation/hash. This
#     profile can read a signed BundleParty extension `identityBundle` (inline) or
#     `identityBundleRef` (storage-program locator and IdentityBundle hash), use the publisher's
#     pinned listing identity when its hash matches, or use EvidenceGraphDeps.resolveIdentityBundle.
#     IdentityBundle hashes omit presentation per DACS-1; a hash alone is not a locator. Missing
#     bytes remain unverified. presentedAt must be numeric but is not a freshness gate. Per-claim Ed25519 presentations are supported by this profile.
#   Required credential matching uses the signed composite generatedAt (unix ms) as the historical
#     Vet instant, bounded by finalisedAt; it does not expire old sessions against the wall clock.
#     validUntil governs; without it, DACS_RECIPE_POLICIES must supply defaultMaxAgeSec for the exact
#     scheme/recipeVersion. Every required result, including one with validUntil, also needs an
#     live exact-version recipe policy, an allowed method and a trusted authenticated signer.
#     RAV-2: the catalog does not disclose per-result availability yet. Non-live vet results
#     remain indeterminate; non-live recipes cannot elevate identity tiers either. This applies
#     to every included VerifyResult, optional ones too: each needs a valid live recipe policy.
#     Wrapper expiry and listing maxAge only narrow that authority window.
#     No scheme-specific requirement-parameter interpreter is configured: non-empty parameters
#     are unmatched, as DACS-1 requires for unrecognised parameters, rather than inferred from data.
#   DV-1..3: storage delivery resolves object cleartext and node ACL metadata. The DV-1 hash covers
#     the complete NFC/JCS payload, including any signature/signatures fields (the pinned SDK's
#     contentHash strips them; the Standard's lifecycle walkthrough does not). Unreadable payloads,
#     encrypt-to-buyer payloads (no buyer decryption capability), and external pointer payloads
#     (no external cleartext resolver) remain indeterminate and never count as completion/volume.
